From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:42:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(delegate): resume a finished subagent with
 action='resume'

A finished background subagent could not take a second round of work; the
parent had to spawn a new one and brief it from its branch and notes.
delegate_task action='resume' (subagent_id, or delegation_id + task_index, and
a message) rebuilds a finished child of the calling chat from its stored
transcript the way a restart handoff does: same goal, route and model,
toolsets, working directory and device binding, its original start time and
tool count carried on. The message is appended as the next user turn and the
child runs as a new background unit with its live transcript and the usual
result re-entry, which reads "Subagent resumed and finished". The unit counts
toward the chat's cap and queues behind it. A running child, a child of another
chat, a nested caller and a child without a finished-run record are refused.

Dispatch stamps each child's session with the record a rebuild needs, and its
finish adds where it ended. It lasts as long as the session: sessions.retention_days
when sessions.auto_prune is on, otherwise until the parent chat is deleted.
